      ":question/problem": "Express the following as a constant multiple of a single trigonometric ratio.\n$$\n2\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{32}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{32}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{32}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{16}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
